<title>FRANCE: Rouen Sept 1-25 grain exports at 298,550 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Rouen Sept 1-25 grain exports at 298,550 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exports from the French port of Rouen reached 298,550 tonnes between September 1 and September 25, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Grain exports totalled 324,000 tonnes in September 1995.</p>
<p>The 298,550 tonnes total included 289,470 tonnes of wheat and 9,080 of barley.</p>
<p>Wheat exports break down as follows (in tonnes)</p>
<p>    West Africa				 33,697</p>
<p>    Canary Islands			     5,150</p>
<p>    Cuba					  43,265</p>
<p>    Denmark					1,500</p>
<p>    Georgia				     25,900</p>
<p>    Britain				     11,950</p>
<p>    Italy					111,306</p>
<p>    Morocco					2,500</p>
<p>    Mauritius				   13,500</p>
<p>    Mozambique				  15,000</p>
<p>    Poland					 8,952</p>
<p>    Portugal				     1,750</p>
<p>    Turkey					15,000</p>
<p>Barley exports break down was follows (in tonnes)</p>
<p>    Belgium					2,800</p>
<p>    Canary Islands			     2,980</p>
<p>    Poland					 3,300</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
